      "reviewer": "Claude Opus 5",
      "reviewedAt": "2026-08-25T13:20:00Z",
      "note": "The anchor is the first of 22 transactions the attacker sent to its module 0x10e5c8d3537856f141272e1c39befdab4dd8bde0, each re-initialising Telcoin wallet clones and sweeping their TEL. The wallet is a minimal proxy of the master 0x10d0e9755c67ab37089acb4f51e8b4ee407fe853, whose 45-byte runtime pins that master, so the clone creation at block 21704647 by the CloneFactory 0x4cf353974155a600f87d73222f9df0548e2b740e is the age basis and the exploited code is 762.3 days old. Neither the factory nor the transaction sender that deployed it is an attacker address. The master itself delegatecalls the address in the wallet’s EIP-1967 beacon slot, which held 0x3f443c31dab3dab882f9fe621f97b74c3c14837d before the exploit and which the re-initialisation overwrote; the defect that made that possible, the unrun initializer, is in victim code that predates all adversarial control and executes in the anchor. Every other drained wallet is a clone of the same master and would group to the same code hash, so one target represents them all. Quantities are netted onchain; the USD figure is the reported realisation because the attacker’s own selling moved TEL 65 percent within five minutes."
    },
